 316               /MAINLINE BASIC (PRIORITY SCHEDULER)
 317               
 318               /WHENEVER THERE IS NOTHING BETTER TO DO
 319               /OR A JOB WANTS TO DISMISS ITSELF SO OTHERS CAN RUN,
 320               /THIS ROUTINE IS ENTERED.
 321               
 322               /IT SEARCHES THE LIST OF USER PRIORITIES FOR THE LOWEST
 323               /PRIORITY LESS THAN 10.  (A PRIORITY > 10 INDICATES I/O WAIT.)
 324               /SERVICING IS ROUND ROBIN WITHIN PRIORITIES.  ONCE SWAPPED IN,
 325               /THE NUMBER OF STATEMENTS THAT THE USER RUNS IS DETERMINED BY
 326               /HIS PRIORITY; THE LOWER THE PRIORITY, THE BIGGER A CHUNCK
 327               /HE GETS.  WHEN A JOB EXITS FROM I/O WAIT, HIS PRIORITY IS
 328               /SET TO 0 (HIGHEST POSSIBLE).  WHEN A JOB USES UP ITS STATEMENT
 329               /ALLOCATION WITHOUT GOING INTO I/O WAIT, ITS PRIORITY IS LOWERED.
 330               /IN THIS WAY, COMPUTE BOUND JOBS GET LARGER CHUNKS OF TIME
 331               /WHILE INTERACTIVE USERS STILL GET A QUICK RESPONSE.
 332               
 333               *177
 334 000177  3022  NULL,   DCA PC          /STORE RESTART ADDRESS
 335 000200  6001          ION             /INTERRUPT ON IN SCHEDULER!!!
 336 000201  2326          ISZ INTCNT      /BUMP COUNT FOR *RANDOMIZE*
 337                       /IN CASE THE ISZ SKIPS
